# 13.0

* [grenade] New experiment description and mapping in grenade 💣
  * network interface is removed and superseeded by Topology-based interface
  * signal_flow.{Graph,Vertex} interface is removed and superseeded by Topology-based interface
  * enables interoperability of the model and hardware graph
  * GreedyMapper:
    * partitioning and placement are performed algorithmically
    * JITCalibration: calibration is performed via calix after partitioning and placement
  * signal_flow.pack_spikes is removed
  * Python-based front end adapter is added
  * Execution{Health,Time}Info are (partially) replaced by ExecutionInstanceGlobal and ExecutorGlobal
  * execution.run can execute hardware/signal_flow-level topologies, mapping from more abstract representations is happening in user code (or the front end adapter) now
* [pynn-brainscales] adapting to grenade
  * preprocess() always requires executor access now. Therefore, we enable using the ZeroMock connection for software tests
  * get_execution_{time,health}_info() is replaced by get_execution_instance_data() -> grenade.common.OutputData.ExecutionInstances
  * Projection.placed_connections return type changes
  * SpikeIOSourcePopulation support is temporarily disabled
* [hxtorch] adapting to grenade
  * PyTorch independent code is moved into core namespace, including:
    * Experiment base class
    * base population and projection
    * Morphology
    * Observables
    * Parameters
    * Calibration helper functions
  * Adds mixin for trainable parameter types
  * Adds an option to enable constant current onto neurons
  * Spilts spiking.types into spiking.types.{population, projection}
  * Removes obsolete NeuronPlacement
  * Removes ExecutionInstance
  * Replaced native calix calibration with cocolist to be more resilient to calix changes
  * Enables projection to either be signed or unsigned
  * Adds plasticity class
  * Drop support for perceptron.InferenceTracer, since not used anymore
* [calix]
  * move CalibrationTargets to C++
    * allows interfacing in e.g. grenade
    * more typesafety
    * dropped non-array supplication of targets
    * change time unit in targets from us to s
    * the target serialization changes, so the calibration
  * cache gets invalidated, since the hash changes. (also applies to nightly deployed calibration)
* [jaxsnn]
  * temporarily drops hardware support

# 12.0

* [brainscales2-demos] adapting to API changes and minor updates (exp. LIF demo and fI-curve, Lui, BSS2 docs, comp. neurosci. demo)
* [calix] optimizations for QuiggeldyConnection; int. cap. char.; inter-comp. conductance, madc char., parallelization of fits
* [fisch] adapt to hxcomm::MultiConnection
* [haldls] multi-chip tests; integration of hxcomm::MultiConnection
* [hxtorch] add ExpSumOverTime decoder; add lead_conductance neuron parameter; minor fixes
* [pynn-brainscales] support for SpikeIO RX (OffChipSource)

# 11.0

* [fisch] provide more debug context when pbmem times out
* [grenade] fixes in MC functionality, CADC recording handling, 
* [halco] Python wrapping fix, some new coordinates
* [haldls] fix MemoryTiming-related issue, add initial support for inter-FPGA routing table
* [hxcomm] support for MultiConnection, better logging
* [hxtorch] add initial PlasticityRule support, support for adapt data, better ADC observables, NIR{,Data} support
* [jaxsnn] support for NIRData
* [pynn-brainscales] support for CADC recording
